data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L2-057_residual_coupling_flow_block/solution/solution.py","content":"import torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n# Match reference numerics: cuDNN/cuBLAS on Ampere default to TF32 for conv/matmul.\ntorch.backends.cuda.matmul.allow_tf32 = True\ntorch.backends.cudnn.allow_tf32 = True\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# c002 — EXACT sequential reference in Triton (correctness-first).\n#\n# c001 assumed x_mask==1 and collapsed the 4 transforms into a single\n# delta = sum_i transform_i(x0). That FAILED all 5 workloads (max_abs ~5e3):\n# the evaluator supplies a NON-TRIVIAL random x_mask, so the reference's\n# `x = x * x_mask` at the end of every layer re-masks the x0 half before it\n# feeds the next transform. The four transforms therefore see progressively\n# masked, DIFFERENT x0 inputs and are NOT independent; layer order matters.\n#\n# This candidate implements the reference literally. Per layer i, in order\n# (0..3 forward / 3..0 reverse), over a mutable work buffer:\n#   x0 = work[:, :96, :]        # current (already-masked from prior layer) buffer\n#   h  = conv2_i(relu(conv1_i(relu(conv0_i(x0)))))    # 96->192->192->96, k=5, pad=2\n#   h *= x_mask\n#   x1 = work[:, 96:, :] (+/-) h\n#   work = cat([x0, x1]) * x_mask\n# Forward (+), layers 0..3; reverse (-), layers 3..0. Output = final work.\n#\n# Conv: implicit-GEMM over (time-tile, cout-tile, batch), tap loop k in 0..4\n# with zero-pad masking (input index t+k-2), TF32 tl.dot (FP32 accumulate),\n# fused +bias and (optional) relu. conv0/conv1 relu; conv2 no relu.","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":251}}}
