ASSED\", \"speedup\": 0.7299497402115508, \"ref_ms\": 1.53049, \"sol_ms\": 2.096706, \"max_abs\": 0.0089111328125, \"max_rel\": 0.0391}, {\"uuid\": \"3c3868a4\", \"wl\": 3, \"B\": 16, \"T\": 2048, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": true, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"speedup\": 0.49158156632110567, \"ref_ms\": 12.404802, \"sol_ms\": 25.234474, \"max_abs\": 0.015625, \"max_rel\": 0.3866}, {\"uuid\": \"84fb0bc5\", \"wl\": 4, \"B\": 2, \"T\": 293, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": true, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"speedup\": 0.5821712597238484, \"ref_ms\": 1.009154, \"sol_ms\": 1.7334315, \"max_abs\": 0.0089111328125, \"max_rel\": 0.0119}, {\"uuid\": \"ea5ae433\", \"wl\": 5, \"B\": 64, \"T\": 8192, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": true, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"speedup\": 0.17425472963887817, \"ref_ms\": 68.092176, \"sol_ms\": 390.762286, \"max_abs\": 0.017578125, \"max_rel\": 0.4229}], \"all_passed\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 0.5026458432077623, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 0.5718769580083973, \"decision\": \"champion\", \"reason\": \"FIRST VALID candidate: 5/5 pass. Precision fix (TF32->FP32) closed the gate exactly as diagnosed - max_abs dropped from c002's ~20 to <=0.018 (all within atol=0.011+rtol*|ref| for >=99% of elements). Becomes standing champion. HOWEVER geomean=0.50x is a SLOWDOWN vs reference (cuDNN). Per-WL: WL1 0.88x, WL2 0.73x, WL4 0.58x, WL3 0.49x, WL5 0.17x. WL5 (B=64,T=8192, compute-bound) is the dominant drag: full-FP32 tl.dot lowers to FMA (no tensor cores) so we lose ~8x vs cuDNN TF32. Root tension: FP32 needed for correctness kills throughput on the big WL. Next levers to beat cuDNN while staying FP32-accurate: (a) reduce kernel/launch count and buffer round-trips (12 conv launches + 4 combine per call); (b) better tiling/num_warps/num_stages, esp. larger tiles + pipelining for WL5; (c) investigate a TF32+FP32-residual correction (3xTF32 / split-K) to reclaim tensor-core throughput while meeting rtol=1e-5. c004 will target tiling+fusion for WL5.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 3, \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki not used (A800/sm_80 Ampere, out of scope); no external tools.\"}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":60985,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":4871,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06e14bc0-8cfa-4bea-9f89-b0d098466548","uuid":"f877cca0-8472-45e6-b72a-169f6a222187","timestamp":"2026-09-17T19:54:36.517Z"}
