launches + 4 combine per call); (b) better tiling/num_warps/num_stages, esp. larger tiles + pipelining for WL5; (c) investigate a TF32+FP32-residual correction (3xTF32 / split-K) to reclaim tensor-core throughput while meeting rtol=1e-5. c004 will target tiling+fusion for WL5.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 3, \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki not used (A800/sm_80 Ampere, out of scope); no external tools.\"}","originalFile":"{\"candidate\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"a15872e97f1e4e8ae3fe94d72ecbdc56fd42179e213f8d521e2a252076c54e53\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-16T18:35:55Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Correctness-first per-transform Triton implicit-GEMM conv (TF32, fused bias/relu, no-relu after conv2) using the draft independence collapse: delta=sum_i transform_i(x0); out1 = mask*(x1 +/- mask*delta); out0 = mask*x0. Assumes x_mask==1 so all 4 transforms read the same unchanging x0.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"root\", \"validation\": {\"signature_ok\": true, \"padding_offset_ok\": true, \"bias_relu_order_ok\": true, \"reverse_sign_ok\": true, \"mask_assumption_ok\": false, \"dtype_ok\": true}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"0e8f2568\", \"wl\": 1, \"B\": 8, \"T\": 1721, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 5518.55, \"max_rel\": 111242.76}, {\"uuid\": \"f274d392\", \"wl\": 2, \"B\": 4, \"T\": 541, \"reverse\": false, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 5108.31, \"max_rel\": 124171.63}, {\"uuid\": \"3c3868a4\", \"wl\": 3, \"B\": 16, \"T\": 2048, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 5432.48, \"max_rel\": 115663.49}, {\"uuid\": \"84fb0bc5\", \"wl\": 4, \"B\": 2, \"T\": 293, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 4470.75, \"max_rel\": 85608.45}, {\"uuid\": \"ea5ae433\", \"wl\": 5, \"B\": 64, \"T\": 8192, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 6099.80, \"max_rel\": 248190.31}], \"all_passed\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"All 5 WLs INCORRECT_NUMERICAL with systematic large errors (max_abs ~4.5e3-6.1e3, max_rel ~1e5), identical scale across every WL. Root cause: the draft's mask==1 independence collapse is invalid. The evaluator supplies a NON-TRIVIAL random x_mask (workloads mark x_mask type=random), so the reference applies x = x*mask at the end of EACH layer, which re-masks x0 before it feeds the next transform. Thus transform_i receive progressively-masked, DIFFERENT x0 inputs; the transforms are not independent and layer order matters. My delta=sum_i transform_i(raw x0) shortcut breaks. Conv padding/bias/relu order and reverse sign logic look correct (errors are structural, not off-by-one). Next candidate (c002) must implement the EXACT sequential reference: keep a working buffer, per layer do conv0->relu->conv1->relu->conv2, then out1=(x1 +/- h*mask)*mask and out0=x0*mask written back, iterating layers 0..3 forward / 3..0 reverse.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 1, \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki not used (A800/sm_80 Ampere, out of scope); no external tools.\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c002\", \"parent\": \"c001\", \"source_sha256\": \"8c42902f87bbbe942a1f6ccb7d7e1447439a9482bd92b9f10fd8b7e865863979\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Implement the EXACT sequential reference in Triton (drop c001's invalid mask==1 independence collapse). Per layer in true order (0..3 fwd / 3..0 rev) over a mutable work buffer: conv0->relu->conv1->relu->conv2 (+bias, no relu after conv2), then in-place fused combine work[:, :96]=mask*x0 and work[:, 96:]=mask*(x1 +/- mask*h). TF32 tl.dot (FP32 accumulate). Expect correctness on all 5 WLs.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"New root of revised lineage. Iterate 4 layers sequentially over a cloned work buffer instead of summing 4 independent transforms of raw x0; apply x_mask after every layer (re-masking x0 before the next transform); combine writes in place to work rather than a separate delta+combine. Conv kernel unchanged (tap offset, bias, relu); removed the ACCUMULATE path.\", \"validation\": {\"signature_ok\": true, \"padding_offset_ok\": true, \"bias_relu_order_ok\": true, \"reverse_sign_ok\": true, \"mask_sequential_ok\": true, \"dtype_ok\": true}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"0e8f2568\", \"wl\": 1, \"B\": 8, \"T\": 1721, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 20.501953125, \"max_rel\": 237.11}, {\"uuid\": \"f274d392\", \"wl\": 2, \"B\": 4, \"T\": 541, \"reverse\": false, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 21.041992, \"max_rel\": 229.06}, {\"uuid\": \"3c3868a4\", \"wl\": 3, \"B\": 16, \"T\": 2048, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 17.236816, \"max_rel\": 308.83}, {\"uuid\": \"84fb0bc5\", \"wl\": 4, \"B\": 2, \"T\": 293, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 17.104004, \"max_rel\": 138.90}, {\"uuid\": \"ea5ae433\", \"wl\": 5, \"B\": 64, \"T\": 8192, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 21.824219, \"max_rel\": 360.34}], \"all_passed\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Structural formula now correct: max_abs collapsed from c001's ~5e3 to ~20 (250x reduction) purely by switching to the exact sequential per-layer mask application, confirming (a) the mask is non-trivial random and (b) layer order matters. Remaining error is uniform (~17-22 max_abs) across ALL five WLs regardless of B*T, i.e. NOT a size-dependent tiling/boundary bug but a global precision gap. The random mask multiplies the work buffer every layer (values grow ~mask^k), and with rtol=1e-5 (200x below TF32's ~2e-3 relative error) large-magnitude elements exceed atol=0.01+rtol*|ref|, so >1% mismatch. Diagnosis: reference is effectively FP32; TF32 tl.dot cannot meet the gate. Next candidate c003 = same exact-sequential structure but FP32 accumulate (ALLOW_TF32=False) to close the precision gap.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 2, \"skill_usage\": \"KernelWiki not used (A800/sm_80 Ampere, out of scope); no external tools.\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":2,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":[" {\"candidate\": \"c001\", \"parent\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"a15872e97f1e4e8ae3fe94d72ecbdc56fd42179e213f8d521e2a252076c54e53\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-16T18:35:55Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Correctness-first per-transform Triton implicit-GEMM conv (TF32, fused bias/relu, no-relu after conv2) using the draft independence collapse: delta=sum_i transform_i(x0); out1 = mask*(x1 +/- mask*delta); out0 = mask*x0. Assumes x_mask==1 so all 4 transforms read the same unchanging x0.\", \"changes_vs_parent\": \"root\", \"validation\": {\"signature_ok\": true, \"padding_offset_ok\": true, \"bias_relu_order_ok\": true, \"reverse_sign_ok\": true, \"mask_assumption_ok\": false, \"dtype_ok\": true}, \"results\": [{\"uuid\": \"0e8f2568\", \"wl\": 1, \"B\": 8, \"T\": 1721, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 5518.55, \"max_rel\": 111242.76}, {\"uuid\": \"f274d392\", \"wl\": 2, \"B\": 4, \"T\": 541, \"reverse\": false, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 5108.31, \"max_rel\": 124171.63}, {\"uuid\": \"3c3868a4\", \"wl\": 3, \"B\": 16, \"T\": 2048, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 5432.48, \"max_rel\": 115663.49}, {\"uuid\": \"84fb0bc5\", \"wl\": 4, \"B\": 2, \"T\": 293, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 4470.75, \"max_rel\": 85608.45}, {\"uuid\": \"ea5ae433\", \"wl\": 5, \"B\": 64, \"T\": 8192, \"reverse\": true, \"passed\": false, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"max_abs\": 6099.80, \"max_rel\": 248190.31}], \"all_pass